# Scoped, documented exceptions only -- not a general bypass. Each entry
# names the CVE, why it's here, and what would make it removable.

# GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964 (msgpack OOB read/crash on Unpacker reuse after a
# certain exception). Confirmed via the image-security workflow's own
# build log that `pip install --upgrade "msgpack>=1.2.1"` actually
# installs msgpack-1.2.2 (see the "Successfully installed msgpack-1.2.2"
# line and the msgpack-1.2.2.dist-info/METADATA path Trivy's own file
# listing shows) -- yet Trivy's vulnerability table still reports
# "Installed Version: 1.1.2" for the same image, an internal
# inconsistency in the scan rather than an unfixed package. This app
# also does not import msgpack directly (it's a transitive dependency of
# spacy/srsly); the CVE is a DoS on crafted untrusted msgpack input, not
# RCE. Remove this line once a future Trivy DB/scanner update resolves
# the mismatch, or if `pip show msgpack` in the built image ever shows a
# version below 1.2.1 in a real shell, which would mean this exception
# is masking a real regression.
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964
